{"title":"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Six distinct positive integers are randomly chosen between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d1216dd3855e1bb88b6136b4ce49c58b57747417.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2006$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" />, inclusive. What is the probability that some pair of these integers has a difference that is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/a/93a5f28e11e150ee277f2f21c8711c4f951e6404.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{1}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(B) } \\frac{3}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(C) } \\frac{2}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(D) } \\frac{4}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 1\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"404\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For two numbers to have a difference that is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the numbers must be congruent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/84027ab631566ed39d8e16d466c9ce6a0b315061.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" /> (their remainders after division by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> must be the same).\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/3/823db59ba5d3dbe69d8abcd62cb81b17cd3ef605.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0, 1, 2, 3, 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" /> are the possible values of numbers in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/84027ab631566ed39d8e16d466c9ce6a0b315061.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" />. Since there are only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible values in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/84027ab631566ed39d8e16d466c9ce6a0b315061.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" /> and we are picking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers, by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pigeonhole_Principle\" title=\"Pigeonhole Principle\">Pigeonhole Principle</a>, two of the numbers must be congruent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/84027ab631566ed39d8e16d466c9ce6a0b315061.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore the probability that some pair of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> integers has a difference that is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/b/c6ba8d576d943711052a5a444c3211a6e555cb57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"56\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/jfkW_KwI9Wo\">https://youtu.be/jfkW_KwI9Wo</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A\">2006 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10